    "https://jobs.drake.edu/jobs/associate-provost-for-faculty-affairs-100089": {
      "title": "Apply for position",
      "description": "Associate Provost for Faculty Affairs - 100089 - Home (current) About Drake Mission & Values Working at Drake Benefits Overview Living in Des Moines Contact Us Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Associate Provost for Faculty Affairs - 100089 Office of the Provost Faculty, non-tenure track Faculty, tenure track Add to favorites View favorites Title: Associate Provost for Faculty Affairs - 100089 Position Number: 100089 Unit/Department: Office of the Provost Salary: Stipend & Course Release Job Summary: The Associate Provost for Faculty Affairs is responsible for managing, operationalizing and supporting faculty-related policies, procedures, and functions. This includes overseeing the Office of Sponsored Programs and Research Compliance, the Center for Teaching and Learning, new faculty hiring and orientation, new chair training, facilitating Academic Chair and Associate Dean meetings, convening a Graduate Council, and serving as the primary liaison between academic departments, the Provost’s Office and Global Affairs to support transnational programs and study abroad, as well as other duties as assigned. This position will report directly to the Provost and will come with no required teaching responsibilities and an additional stipend. The initial term is for three years and can be renewed. Minimum Qualifications: • Associate Professor or Full Professor at Drake University • Administrative experience at Drake University (program coordinator, committee chair, director, department chair, associate dean, etc.) • Demonstrated ability to successfully complete work independently and on a group/committee • Demonstrated record of published research • Stated commitment to Drake University mission and core values • Ability to handle sensitive/confidential information with appropriate care • Experience managing a budget Preferred Qualifications: • Tenured faculty member at Drake University • Experience successfully leading and working on teams • Strong interpersonal communication skills • Strong written communication skills • Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously • Capacity to analyze complex data and problems Job Duties: Oversee Office of Sponsored Programs and Research Compliance Supervise and ensure delivery of programming through the Center for Teaching and Learning Support faculty development and faculty awards efforts/programming Convene Academic Chairs/Associate Dean meetings Serve as primary point of contact for faculty, deans, and departments with transnational program implementation and management Assist in hiring of global faculty Support visa efforts for faculty Engage in strategic planning for program growth Support Drake-deployed faculty Provide other academic support to departments, colleges, faculty and Global Affairs as needed Create and convene Graduate Council Oversee the University Honors Program and its director Receive and review sabbatical reports Serve ex-officio on: University Curriculum Committee (UCC) Admission, Retention, and Financial Aid Committee (ARFAC) Assessment Committee Assist with development and implementation of academic policies Manage the Faculty and Chair Handbook in collaboration with other relevant groups Coordinate First-Year Seminar Program Engage on curricular issues with faculty Other duties as assigned Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications due:  September 18, 2026 Required Materials: Cover Letter, CV, list of two Drake-affiliated references Review of Applications Begins: Applications due:  September 18, 2026 For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. ABOUT DRAKE Drake University is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. As reflected in our Core Values, we embrace a diverse and inclusive community. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY Drake University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. We provide equal employment opportunities to all individuals regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law.  Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (p: 515.271.3133; e: jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. Apply Now Sign up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 369eeac9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Office of the Provost Office of the Provost First Name (required) 5024c1bd Last Name (required) 2a784405 Email (required) abf439f8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 8e8158d3 Last Name (required) e7145d53 Email (required) 5d5a0a9c Please enter the information of the person you would like to share this job with 509618fc Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply for position First Name (required) 0d7952cf Last Name (required) 665d0a56 Email (required) 8847aa7e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 2507 University Ave.   Des Moines, IA 50311 515-271-2011 Maps & Directions University Calendar Contact Directory Public Safety VISIT APPLY REQUEST INFO About Drake Academics Admission Campus Life Online Athletics Alumni News & Events Giving College of Arts & Sciences Zimpleman College of Business John Dee Bright College School of Education School of Journalism & Mass Communication Law School College of Pharmacy & Health Sciences Cowles Library Employment Giving to Drake COVID-19: Our Response Information Technology Services Consumer Information Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Nondiscrimination & Accessibility Privacy Statement Do Not Sell My Information © 2022 Drake University. All rights reserved. Candidate Details Please choose the department(s)"
