    "https://jobs.drake.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-athletics-marketing-998965": {
      "title": "Apply for position",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing - 998965 - Home (current) About Drake Mission & Values Working at Drake Benefits Overview Living in Des Moines Contact Us Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing - 998965 Athletic Marketing Staff, full-time (32+ hours per week) Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing - 998965 Position Number: 998965 Unit/Department: Athletic Marketing Salary: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Department Summary: Drake University's Athletics Department competes in the Missouri Valley Conference at the NCAA Division I level. Bulldog student-athletes thrive in the classroom and their respective field of play. Drake Athletics sport programs are considered Des Moines’ Hometown Team. The department culture is predicated on a common value statement known as The Bulldog Way written by coaches, staff, and student-athletes. This intentional commitment to a championship culture is led by integrity, excellence, wanting the best for and best from one another, and aspiring to greatness provides a foundation for student-athletes, coaches, and athletics staff to study, work, and play. Job Summary: Drake Athletics is seeking a qualified candidate to fill the opening of Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing. Reporting to the Director of Athletics Marketing, the Assistant Director will be responsible for developing, implementing and executing a comprehensive marketing and ticket sales plan for sports as assigned. The Assistant Director also utilizes official social media platforms and assists in overseeing email marketing campaigns to engage fans by delivering entertaining and informative content and is charged with administering a campus marketing strategy to increase student engagement. This position will work nights, weekends, and possibly holidays. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, sports management, business, public relations or a related field (Required.) • At least one (1) year of relevant experience in collegiate athletics, professional sports, event marketing, sports marketing or a comparable environment. Graduate assistant, internship and significant student-worker experience may count toward this requirement. • Demonstrated experience assisting with or executing athletics marketing, fan engagement, promotions or game presentation. • Ability to develop and execute marketing and promotional plans designed to increase attendance, enhance the fan experience and support ticket revenue goals. • Experience coordinating game-day elements such as promotions, scripts, music, in-venue entertainment, student engagement, spirit groups, giveaways and special presentations. • Ability to manage multiple projects, events and deadlines simultaneously in a fast-paced environment. • Strong written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with coaches, student-athletes, staff, students, vendors and external partners. • Demonstrated organizational skills and attention to detail. • Ability to supervise, schedule and provide direction to student workers and game-day personnel. • Working knowledge of digital and social media platforms (Facebook, Instagram, and X) and their application to sports marketing and fan engagement. • Proficiency with standard workplace productivity tools, including Microsoft Office and/or Google Workspace. • Ability and willingness to work nights, weekends and holidays as required by the intercollegiate athletics schedule. • Commitment to the standards and values of Drake University, the Missouri Valley Conference, Pioneer Football League and NCAA. • Valid driver’s license and ability to travel locally as required. Preferred Qualifications: • Two (2) or more years of progressively responsible experience in collegiate athletics, professional sports or a comparable sports/event marketing environment. • Previous experience serving as the primary marketing or game-presentation contact for one or more sports, teams or major events. • Demonstrated experience developing and executing comprehensive marketing plans that support attendance, ticket sales, fan engagement, brand awareness and revenue-generation goals. • Previous experience with email marketing, including development of targeted campaigns, audience segmentation, content creation, data analytics, scheduling and evaluation of campaign performance. • Experience with digital advertising platforms, including paid social media, search, display or other audience-targeted advertising campaigns. • Experience developing and executing promotions, theme nights, giveaways, community-engagement initiatives and other strategies designed to enhance the fan experience. • Experience writing and coordinating game scripts, run-of-show documents, in-venue promotions and other game-presentation elements. • Previous experience managing special events, including coordination of vendors, contractors, permits, budgets, event logistics and promotional plans. • Experience recruiting, scheduling, training and supervising student employees, interns, volunteers or game-day staff. • Experience working collaboratively with ticket sales, athletics communications, video production, corporate partnerships, development and other external-facing units within an athletics organization. • Experience working directly with coaches and sport administrators to establish marketing priorities to develop and execute sport-specific promotional plans. • Experience coordinating spirit squads, bands, mascots, student organizations or other groups that contribute to game atmosphere and fan engagement. • Working knowledge of ticketing and customer relationship management systems and the use of audience data to support marketing and ticket-sales strategies. • Experience using analytics and performance metrics to evaluate marketing campaigns, attendance initiatives and fan-engagement efforts. • Familiarity with graphic design, content-creation or project-management platforms such as Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, Asana or comparable tools. • Demonstrated ability to build productive relationships with campus organizations, community partners, vendors and other external stakeholders. • Experience managing budgets, processing invoices and purchase orders, negotiating with vendors and tracking expenditures. • Knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations and previous experience working within an NCAA Division I athletics department preferred. • Demonstrated creativity, initiative and ability to independently identify opportunities to grow attendance, improve the fan experience and strengthen the connection between an athletics program and its campus and community. Job Duties: 20% - Develop and execute comprehensive marketing and ticket sales strategies for assigned sports in collaboration with the Director of Athletics Marketing and Athletics Ticketing, with an emphasis on increasing revenue, raising attendance, and enhancing in-game promotions to maximize the fan experience. - (Essential) 20% - Lead athletics marketing game-day operations for assigned home athletic events, including event scripting, promotional activities, contests, music, and other fan engagement initiatives. Coordinate with corporate sales and event partners to ensure successful execution of sponsorship activations and promotional elements while delivering a consistent and engaging fan experience. - (Essential) 15% - Develop and execute marketing focused social media content and campaigns for assigned sports and designated department properties, including the Drake Relays, Drake Road Races and Grand Blue Mile, in collaboration with Athletics Communications and the Director of Athletics Marketing. Manage the development, execution and scheduling of athletics email marketing campaigns, including audience segmentation, content development, creative coordination and performance analysis, to drive ticket sales, attendance, fan engagement and revenue. - (Essential) 15% - Develop and coordinate promotional creative assets for email, digital, social media, in-venue and other marketing channels utilizing department templates and collaborating with contracted designers and internal creative resources as appropriate. - (Essential) 15% - Develop and execute an on-campus student engagement plan designed to increase student awareness, attendance and participation at Drake Athletics events. Build relationships with student organizations, campus departments and student leaders to develop creative initiatives and promotions. - (Essential) 10% - In collaboration with the Director of Athletics Marketing, hire student mascot performers. Once hired manage scheduling and training program. Oversee and manage the student intern program. This includes hiring, scheduling, training, and day-to-day oversight. - (Essential) 5% - Other duties as assigned - (Essential) Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants will be asked to complete the online application through Drake's job board and provide: a resume/cv, a cover, and contact information for three references. Have Questions? Question about the application process, working at Drake, reasonable accommodations, benefits, or additional information about Drake or Des Moines, Iowa may be directed to Drake Human Resources. You can best reach us at jobs@drake.edu . All job offers are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check, satisfactory reference checks, and proof of work authorization. Review of Applications Begins: A review of applications will begin immediately. This position will remain open until filled. Salary and Benefits: At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our Drake Benefits Guide 2026 . One of our popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. Tuition Benefits For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. ABOUT DRAKE Drake University is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. As reflected in our Core Values, we embrace a diverse and inclusive community. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY Drake University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. We provide equal employment opportunities to all individuals regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law.  Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (p: 515.271.3133; e: jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. Apply Now Sign up for Job Alerts! Job Alert c3c39967 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Athletic Marketing Athletic Marketing First Name (required) 9b4b0915 Last Name (required) 78709810 Email (required) 96084724 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) a0e7082d Last Name (required) 9c226191 Email (required) d6167fbb Please enter the information of the person you would like to share this job with 40d63213 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply for position First Name (required) 1cb7c7f7 Last Name (required) 5ee57284 Email (required) 15fa84c6 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 2507 University Ave.   Des Moines, IA 50311 515-271-2011 Maps & Directions University Calendar Contact Directory Public Safety VISIT APPLY RE