    "https://jobs.drake.edu/jobs/admission-support-specialist-999911-05ab5646-5604-49c1-b077-5289234868f5": {
      "title": "Apply for position",
      "description": "Admission Support Specialist - 999911 - Home (current) About Drake Mission & Values Working at Drake Benefits Overview Living in Des Moines Contact Us Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Admission Support Specialist - 999911 Staff, full-time (32+ hours per week) Add to favorites View favorites Title: Admission Support Specialist - 999911 Position Number: 999911 Unit/Department: Admissions & Enrollment Salary: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Department Summary: Drake University's Office of Admission is responsible for enrolling the University's vibrant, talented, and diverse undergraduate students. Led by the Dean of Admission and in collaboration with a team of talented professionals, this department works in conjunction with campus partners to identify and recruit future Bulldogs (students, not actual bulldogs) both in the state of Iowa and across the United States. Job Summary: The Office of Admission seeks a dynamic individual to join our amazing team. We are hiring for an Admission Support Specialist to manage the department’s budget and provide an array of administrative assistance to Admission leadership and the overall office. The Admission Support Specialist wears a number of hats within the Office of Admission, chief among these hats is the role of budget manager. This Admission Support Specialist will oversee the department’s budget in conjunction with the dean of admission and ensure the Office of Admission remains fiscally responsible in execution of its primary focus of outreach to and recruitment of undergraduate students (first-year, transfer, and Bright College). The Admission Support Specialist will review P-card purchases, ensure invoices are settled, and serve as the primary liaison to the University’s Accounting division. The Admission Support Specialist will also meet regularly (weekly) with the dean of admission and produce monthly budget reports for review. In addition to the budget management responsibilities, the Admission Support Specialist will also oversee a variety of administrative duties including supporting the dean of admission and other admission leaders, as needed, assisting with bi-weekly staff meetings, managing Office of Admission calendars, ordering office/clerical supplies needed for the Office of Admission, managing deliveries/packages, assisting with the onboarding of new staff, serving as the primary building manager (Cole Hall), and providing coverage and support to the Campus Visit Team within the Office of Admission. The Admission Support Specialist is the backbone of the Office of Admission. As a result, we are looking for someone responsible, trustworthy, and dependable with good interpersonal skills. This individual should have great attention to detail, excellent communication skills, and the ability to adapt to change (as the work of recruitment is constantly evolving). Minimum Qualifications: • Associate degree • Ability to work independently and effectively while managing multiple initiatives • Outstanding attention to detail • Excellent time management skills • Great interpersonal skills • A positive and professional attitude Preferred Qualifications: • Bachelor degree • Prior experience in budget management and/or understanding basic bookkeeping/accounting with a strong commitment to confidentiality • Prior experience as an office manager or administrative assistant • Experience in a higher education or other non-profit environment Job Duties: 50% - Budget Manager: Manage, organize, prepare, and maintain the office budget and other financial records using a variety of formats for data compilation, manipulation, and display. Prepare monthly budget reports and other financial spreadsheets for the Dean of Admission and other administrators as required. Serve as liaison with university accounting and facilitate staff submission of travel expense reports, direct payments, and credit card reporting. Prepare and submit payments of projects, contracts, and services to university accounting. Requires maintaining and controlling confidentiality of files, as necessary. - (Essential) 20% - Administrative Support: Provide administrative support to the Dean of Admission (75%) and other admissions leadership staff (25%) as needed. Prepare bi-weekly staff meetings including agendas, meeting slides, scheduling meeting guests, and preparing minute takers. Maintain departmental records. Assist with onboarding process for new admission staff. Requires maintaining and controlling confidentiality of files, as necessary. - (Essential) 15% - Office/Building Manager: Serve as a contact for Admission regarding building maintenance including electronics, heating, cooling, office moves, cleaning and other general maintenance and repairs; also including electronic/technology needs and other work orders. Complete work orders as requested for facilities repair and maintenance. Coordinate, order and manage supply ordering (Office Max, Amazon, and other vendors); Receive and ensure delivery of mail and packages; Manage UPS shipping. Supervise multifunction machines. Plan, coordinate, and execute complex administrative projects to support the business of onboarding staff, ordering and approving business cards, name badges, and office name plates. Complete room reservations; coordinate scheduling of meetings, reserving equipment for presentations as necessary; coordinate staff candidate interview itineraries. - (Essential) 15% - Campus Visit Support: Represent the university and the Office of Admission in welcoming prospective students and families to the university. Provide coverage on scheduled work-from-home (WFH) days and/or vacation days for the Campus Visit Coordinator and campus visit team (CVT) by fulfilling campus visit duties. - (Essential) % - Perform other duties, as assigned. - (Essential) Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter. If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email joel.johnson@drake.edu Review of Applications Begins: A review of applications will begin immediately.  This position will remain open until filled. Salary and Benefits: At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our Drake Benefits Guide 2026 . One of our popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. Tuition Benefits For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. ABOUT DRAKE Drake University is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. As reflected in our Core Values, we embrace a diverse and inclusive community. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY Drake University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. We provide equal employment opportunities to all individuals regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law.  Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (p: 515.271.3133; e: jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. Apply Now Sign up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 7b48f138 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments First Name (required) 7090198c Last Name (required) 2b3db6b7 Email (required) e721cdde Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 285ee78a Last Name (required) 00f3dde4 Email (required) 8aecb3b1 Please enter the information of the person you would like to share this job with 4ab90ff6 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply for position First Name (required) 81f72ce5 Last Name (required) 2f17b160 Email (required) e1877b3c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 2507 University Ave.   Des Moines, IA 50311 515-271-2011 Maps & Directions University Calendar Contact Directory Public Safety VISIT APPLY REQUEST INFO About Drake Academics Admission Campus Life Online Athletics Alumni News & Events Giving College of Arts & Sciences Zimpleman College of Business John Dee Bright College School of Education School of Journalism & Mass Communication Law School College of Pharmacy & Health Sciences Cowles Library Employment Giving to Drake COVID-19: Our Response Information Technology Services Consumer Information Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Nondiscrimination & Accessibility Privacy Statement Do Not Sell My Information © 2022 Drake University. All rights reserved. Candidate Details Please choose the department(s)"
