    "https://jobs.drake.edu/jobs/cphs-office-and-external-relations-manager-999273": {
      "title": "Apply for position",
      "description": "CPHS Office and External Relations Manager - 999273 - Home (current) About Drake Mission & Values Working at Drake Benefits Overview Living in Des Moines Contact Us Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me CPHS Office and External Relations Manager - 999273 Dean's Office Pharmacy & HS Staff, full-time (32+ hours per week) Add to favorites View favorites Title: CPHS Office and External Relations Manager - 999273 Position Number: 999273 Unit/Department: Dean's Office Pharmacy & HS Salary: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Job Summary: The Drake University College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences seeks a highly organized manager for office operations and external relations in a multi-faceted position working with college administrators, alumni, external stakeholders, faculty, staff, and students. The Office and External Relations Manager reports directly to the Dean of the College. This position functions as the primary office and external relations manager for the College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences with responsibilities for oversight of activities consistent with the established goals and objectives in the areas of administration and alumni/external stakeholders. The functions include providing executive administrative assistant support for the Dean, supervision of Dean’s administrative staff, oversight of events and other external relations; assistance in alumni and advancement efforts; and facilitation of the continuing improvement plan and operational efficiencies. As a key member of the College’s leadership, the Office and External Relations Manager is expected to actively engage in internal and external affairs and serves on the leadership team for the College. Active engagement and creative leadership for the program is expected. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required; Master’s degree preferred. 1 -3 years work experience required; higher education experience preferred. Experience with Workday preferred Preferred Qualifications: Computer skills at intermediate level with Microsoft Office and database entry. Ability to operate multi-function printing, scanning and fax machines and to multi-task highly desired. Preferred skills include excellent problem-solving skills, oral and written communication skills, project initiative, independent decision making, and supervision of administrative staff and student employees. Job Duties: 25% - Executive Support: Functions as a representative for and an assistant to the Dean regarding a variety of tasks making independent judgments and decisions necessary in that role. Assist and support the Dean with any initiatives deemed necessary. Coordinate and prioritize the work of the Dean to include daily work and appointments; maintain and update required college files, records and publications; review material for typographical accuracy, format, conformance with procedures, internal consistency, and ensure proper approvals have been obtained before releasing correspondence. Directs communications manager to post appropriate materials for the Dean’s Office on the college website. - (Essential) 25% - Event Management: Conceptualize, develop, facilitate, and implement good public, alumni, and community relations. Manage events (Medal of Honor Lecture, Alumni Awards, Reunions, Receptions, White and Blue Coat Ceremonies, Pinning Ceremonies, Commencement Ceremony, etc.) that highlight the College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences to the University, current and prospective students and families, health care community, and surrounding neighbors in conjunction with Dean, major gift officer, alumni relations personnel, college alumni, and special events personnel. Organize and host receptions and meals, coordinate videotaping, photography, and publicity in coordination with other offices of the University including University Communications and Marketing. - (Essential) 25% - Office Management: Represent the staff as a member of the College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences College Administrative Committee. Work collaboratively with the Dean, faculty, and staff in planning and overseeing the administration of all college matters and college building needs. Implement programs and develop policies and procedures to ensure the attainment of the College’s continuous improvement plan and vision in conjunction with the College Dean and College Administrative Committee. Serve as the recorder for meeting minutes of the College Administrative Committee, faculty meetings, staff meetings, and other management meetings as requested. Organize and lead quarterly staff meetings for all CPHS staff. Manage all official college handbooks/guides and policies required for college governance. Handle the Promotion and Tenure process with the Dean for eligible faculty. Update, organize, approve permissions, and maintain online Teams channels and folders. Secure training for new employees on all databases. Approve and manage access permissions for Qualtrics and Outlook calendars. - (Essential) 15% - External Relations: Coordinate the work and develop/maintain relationships with the College's National Advisory Council and other advisory boards, including the scheduling of meetings, compiling agendas, and distributing minutes. Responsible for overseeing communications with alumni and health care professional communities. As needed, assist with other communications including anticipating, writing, revising, and sending correspondence on behalf of the Dean and college. Ensure that key established relationships are well managed across the College and work with the Dean to foster new relationships with external stakeholders. Uphold a high level of professionalism when interacting with all external stakeholders. - (Essential) 10% - Personnel Management: Provide leadership, management and vision necessary to ensure that the College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences has proper operational controls, administrative and reporting procedures, and personnel systems in place to operate effectively and efficiently. Supervise and direct the work of the Dean's staff including the Cline and Fitch Administrative Assistants and the Communications Manager. Ensure the smooth workflow and division/delegation of tasks. Monitor process and approve employment time cards, vacation, performance goals and evaluations of all direct reports. Hold regular meetings with direct reports to assess workload and staffing needs. In coordination with the Budget Manager, manage onboarding processes for all new staff and faculty hired within CPHS, including submitting IT and facilities requests, securing appropriate trainings for new hires, and serving as an onboarding support resource. Performs other duties as assigned. - (Essential) Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter. If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email diana.newman@drake.edu Review of Applications Begins: A review of applications will begin immediately.  This position will remain open until filled. Salary and Benefits: At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our Drake Benefits Guide 2026 . One of our popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. Tuition Benefits For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. ABOUT DRAKE Drake University is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. As reflected in our Core Values, we embrace a diverse and inclusive community. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY Drake University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. We provide equal employment opportunities to all individuals regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law.  Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (p: 515.271.3133; e: jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. Apply Now Sign up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 69f51be2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Dean's Office Pharmacy & HS Dean's Office Pharmacy & HS First Name (required) ac5e38fd Last Name (required) a780e894 Email (required) 93747d80 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 035d05b3 Last Name (required) 0fcb0555 Email (required) c769e3cb Please enter the information of the person you would like to share this job with 2a4fcd72 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply for position First Name (required) f6a0b989 Last Name (required) 1c7a2163 Email (required) 0fe9287c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 2507 University Ave.   Des Moines, IA 50311 515-271-2011 Maps & Directions University Calendar Contact Directory Public Safety VISIT APPLY REQUEST INFO About Drake Academics Admission Campus Life Online Athletics Alumni News & Events Giving College of Arts & Sciences Zimpleman College of Business John Dee Bright College School of Education School of Journalism & Mass Communication Law School College of Pharmacy & Health Sciences Cowles Library Employment Giving to Drake COVID-19: Our Response Information Technology Services Consumer Information Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Nondiscrimination & Accessibility Privacy Statement Do Not Sell My Information © 2022 Drake University. All rights reserved. Candidate Details Please choose the department(s)"
