    "https://jobs.drake.edu/jobs/cphs-administrative-assistant-2-998299": {
      "title": "Apply for position",
      "description": "CPHS Administrative Assistant 2 - 998299 - Home (current) About Drake Mission & Values Working at Drake Benefits Overview Living in Des Moines Contact Us Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me CPHS Administrative Assistant 2 - 998299 Dean's Office Pharmacy & HS Staff, full-time (32+ hours per week) Add to favorites View favorites Title: CPHS Administrative Assistant 2 - 998299 Position Number: 998299 Unit/Department: Dean's Office Pharmacy & HS Salary: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Department Summary: The Drake University College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences is excited to hire a highly organized administrative assistant who will excel in a multi-faceted position working with college administrators, faculty, staff and students. This position will supervise student employees, facilitate room scheduling, manage use of instructional equipment, and complete other similar office tasks. Excellent problem-solving skills, oral and written communication skills as well as the ability to demonstrate initiative and independent decision-making skills meeting multiple deadlines is necessary. Position requires the development of a thorough knowledge of College and University policies and procedures. Position requires the establishment of a collegial, collaborative working relationship with administrators, faculty, staff and students. Job Summary: 45% College Administrative Support: Serve as the first level of communication, answering questions from office visitors and current or prospective students. Assist with scheduling and preparing for prospective student visits. Provide basic office support including front desk coverage, filtering voicemails and inquiries to appropriate faculty and staff. Assist with copying, electronic scanning, electronic filing/organization, and maintaining office equipment. Update and maintain College calendars. Manage College room reservations. Assist external visitors with parking requests. Facilitate ordering of office supplies by sending needs to CPHS Budget Manager for ordering. Maintain college loaner computers and instructional equipment, ensuring timely and appropriate updates throughout the year and coordinating reservations. Manage and disperse College mail and packages. Assist with hiring and onboarding processes by assisting with scheduling interview itineraries and ordering of business cards, name badges, and office name plates. Coordinate poster printing for faculty, staff and students for research and educational posters as well as capstone projects. Serve as a backup for College meetings and minutes if needed. Assist with college events and special projects as assigned. 15% Faculty/Departmental Support: Schedule and attend department meetings, disseminate agendas, prepare and distribute meeting minutes, and maintain and archive appropriate departmental records. Secure room reservations and reserve equipment for faculty as necessary. 15% Building Manager: Serve as a contact for the College regarding building maintenance including electronics, heating, cooling, office moves, cleaning and other general maintenance and repairs; also including electronic/technology needs and other work orders. Complete work orders as requested for facilities repair and maintenance. Attend facility meetings. 15% Supervise Student Employees: In coordination with the CPHS Budget Manager and University Human Resources, utilize online recruiting platform, graphic design tools and digital signage platform to recruit and hire work-study students for the College. Ensure the work-study training manual is updated annually with accurate job duties and reference materials. Create semesterly schedules and supervise the workload of student workers. Assign tasks to student workers as appropriate and approve student worker timecards. 5% Communications Support: Send College-wide communication and correspondence as necessary. In coordination with the CPHS Communications Manager, utilize graphic design tools to create posters and maintain and update college digital signage platform. 5% Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications: • Associate or bachelor’s degree • 1-3 years’ work experience • Excellent oral and written communication skills • Proficiency with email, calendars, scheduling appointments and meetings • Ability to operate multi-function printing, scanning and fax machines Preferred Qualifications: • Higher education experience • Basic accounting skills and budget knowledge • Experience and proficiency using Microsoft Office products (Outlook, Word, Excel, Power Point, TEAMS) and Adobe Acrobat • Supervisory experience • Problem-solving, oral and written communication, project initiative and management, independent decision making, and multi-tasking skills Job Duties: 45% - College Administrative Support - (Essential) 15% - Faculty/Departmental Support - (Essential) 15% - Building Manager - (Essential) 15% - Supervise Student Employees - (Essential) 5% - Communications Support - (Essential) 5% - Other duties as assigned - (Essential) Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter. If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email shelby.nelson@drake.edu Review of Applications Begins: A review of applications will begin immediately.  This position will remain open until filled. Salary and Benefits: At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our Drake Benefits Guide 2026 . One of our popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. Tuition Benefits For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. ABOUT DRAKE Drake University is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. As reflected in our Core Values, we embrace a diverse and inclusive community. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY Drake University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. We provide equal employment opportunities to all individuals regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law.  Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (p: 515.271.3133; e: jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. Apply Now Sign up for Job Alerts! Job Alert ee62809b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Dean's Office Pharmacy & HS Dean's Office Pharmacy & HS First Name (required) e2fe99ff Last Name (required) f48554a1 Email (required) 5c0ca9cf Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 02a24926 Last Name (required) d8f52d4f Email (required) 3b9fd9a6 Please enter the information of the person you would like to share this job with 17726062 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply for position First Name (required) 5e2b35bc Last Name (required) 4f942561 Email (required) d086aff7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 2507 University Ave.   Des Moines, IA 50311 515-271-2011 Maps & Directions University Calendar Contact Directory Public Safety VISIT APPLY REQUEST INFO About Drake Academics Admission Campus Life Online Athletics Alumni News & Events Giving College of Arts & Sciences Zimpleman College of Business John Dee Bright College School of Education School of Journalism & Mass Communication Law School College of Pharmacy & Health Science